[Chapter "Sidelines"]
[Line "Maróczy / Fantasy (3.f3)"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Maróczy Variation"]

{White props up e4 with the f-pawn. It is aggressive but costs development.} 1. e4 c6 {Prepares ...d5, so Black can challenge the centre with a pawn while the c8 bishop keeps its diagonal open.} 2. d4 d5 {The point of the Caro-Kann: hit e4 straight away, backed up by the c6 pawn.} 3. f3 {Support e4 with a pawn.} 3... e6 {Solid: if White takes on d5, Black recaptures with the pawn.} 4. Nc3 Bb4 {Pin the knight and add pressure on e4.} 5. Bf4 Ne7 {Develop without allowing e4–e5 to gain time on the knight.} *
